From 49554153d194a7126ee4edf2082e0e7f59a482f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 04:11:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] player information: what its overview page says is decided in
 one tested header
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The overview page of the player information (key O) is to say, in one
sentence, whether the video plays as intended and, if not, what is wrong
and what to do about it. A skin cannot pick the first of ten conditions by
severity without evaluating all of them on every frame, and the same
decision has to hold in every skin, so it is made in C++ and the skin draws
it.

utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h holds, without anything of Kodi in it so that a
test runs it on the host:

- the sentence: the notes that apply, most serious first, in the order of
  the table within a severity, with the number or reason that the sentence
  has in it, what to do, and how many notes there are besides the first
  (Decide(), Notes(), TodoForReason(), HeadCode());
- whether the refresh rate of the display fits the video's (FitRate()),
  where 23.976 fps at 24 Hz is "near" and not a judder anyone sees;
- the text badges of the formats ("Dolby Vision · FEL", "TrueHD Atmos
  7.1.2"), in plain text and not as the logos of the owners of the names;
- the speakers that a layout lights (Speakers()), from the channels of the
  audio engine or the bed of an object-based stream;
- the table of the metadata levels (file, used, sent), with which levels
  Hades acts on read from dvbridge_metadata.h and dvbridge_placebo.c
  (LevelUsed());
- the name and colour of the picture as the decoder gives it, with
  "assumed" where Kodi chose the primaries by the size of the picture;
- the values that changed a moment ago (CChangeFlash), lit for 750 ms of
  the two beats a second that publish them.
---
 xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h | 717 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 717 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h

diff --git a/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h b/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..035e549
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xbmc/utils/HadesPlayerInfo.h
@@ -0,0 +1,717 @@
